## Claim
Text: "Rock musician Jon Bon Jovi performed for 12 people and 7 pumpkins at a campaign event for Democratic presidential nominee Joe Biden in Pennsylvania."
Claim date: October 25, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### Did rock musician Jon Bon Jovi perform at a campaign event for Democratic presidential nominee Joe Biden in Pennsylvania on or around October 24, 2020?
Answer: Yes, according to a Biden campaign report from Friday, October 23, 2020, the rock musician was "set to campaign this weekend with Democratic presidential nominee Joe Biden in Pennsylvania."

Source URL: https://boingboing.net/2020/10/23/bon-jovi-to-campaign-with-joe-biden.html

### What was the specific city, venue, and format of the Joe Biden campaign event featuring Jon Bon Jovi in Pennsylvania in October 2020?
Answer: According to the search result, the Joe Biden campaign event featuring Jon Bon Jovi took place in Dallas, Pennsylvania, and was formatted as a "drive-in rally" where hundreds of supporters listened and honked their horns from their cars. However, the provided text does not specify the exact venue within Dallas where the event was held.

Source URL: https://www.nbcphiladelphia.com/news/politics/decision-2020/bon-jovi-plays-at-biden-event-after-candidate-visits-bucks-county/2572756/

### Was the Joe Biden campaign event featuring Jon Bon Jovi in Pennsylvania in October 2020 structured as a drive-in rally with social distancing guidelines due to the COVID-19 pandemic?
Answer: Yes, the campaign event in Pennsylvania was structured as a drive-in rally that incorporated COVID-19 safety measures. According to the search result, Jon Bon Jovi joined Joe and Jill Biden at a "drive-in campaign event in Pennsylvania's Luzerne County" on October 24, 2020, where attendees honked their car horns. The use of masks was also emphasized at the event, with Bon Jovi pulling down his mask to speak and stating, “Joe knows that masks are not a sign of weakness, they’re a sign of strength.”

Source URL: https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/music/2020/10/24/jon-bon-jovi-hitting-campaign-trail-big-i-vote-concert-support-biden/6022327002/

### Did mainstream news organizations or local journalists report on the crowd size at the Joe Biden campaign event featuring Jon Bon Jovi in Pennsylvania in October 2020?
Answer: Yes, mainstream news organizations reported on the event and indicated a much larger turnout than the claim suggests. Specifically, NBC Philadelphia reported on the drive-in rally in Pennsylvania, noting that Joe Biden delivered a speech "as hundreds of cars honked their horns in approval."

Source URL: https://www.nbcphiladelphia.com/news/politics/decision-2020/bon-jovi-plays-at-biden-event-after-candidate-visits-bucks-county/2572756/

## Final Judgement
### Summary of Key Insights
The recorded evidence shows that rock musician Jon Bon Jovi did perform at a campaign event for Joe Biden in Dallas, Pennsylvania, on October 24, 2020. However, the event was structured as a socially distanced drive-in rally due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Mainstream news reports indicate that the turnout was much larger than the claim suggests, with "hundreds of cars" of supporters attending and honking their horns in approval. Because the evidence clearly shows a substantial turnout of hundreds of vehicles rather than a tiny group, no further investigation is required.

### Conclusion
Based on the retrieved evidence, the claim that Jon Bon Jovi performed for only 12 people and 7 pumpkins is false. The event was a drive-in rally with hundreds of cars in attendance, making the claim's depiction of the crowd size inaccurate. Therefore, the final decision is `refuted`.

### Verdict: REFUTED

### Justification
Rock musician Jon Bon Jovi performed alongside Joe and Jill Biden at a campaign event in Dallas, Pennsylvania, on October 24, 2020, as previewed by [Boing Boing](https://boingboing.net/2020/10/23/bon-jovi-to-campaign-with-joe-biden.html). According to [App.com](https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/music/2020/10/24/jon-bon-jovi-hitting-campaign-trail-big-i-vote-concert-support-biden/6022327002/), the event was structured as a socially distanced drive-in rally with strict COVID-19 safety measures. Reports from [NBC Philadelphia](https://www.nbcphiladelphia.com/news/politics/decision-2020/bon-jovi-plays-at-biden-event-after-candidate-visits-bucks-county/2572756/) confirm that the turnout was substantial, with hundreds of supporters attending in their cars and honking in approval, which refutes the assertion of an extremely small audience.